    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinguish carefully between East-flowing rivers (which form deltas) and West-flowing rivers like Narmada and Tapti (which form estuaries).",
        "Under the Indus Water Treaty of 1960, India gets exclusive rights over the Eastern Rivers (Ravi, Beas, Sutlej), while Pakistan receives the Western Rivers (Indus, Jhelum, Chenab).",
        "Memorize the left-bank and right-bank tributaries of both the Ganga and Brahmaputra, as matching questions appear frequently in Prelims."
      ],
      "id": "uwuhgu0"
